# credentials — never commit an imported token blob
*.token.json
credentials.json

# Working material, all of it kept outside this repo in ~/Personal/ai-usage-companion-notes:
#
#   docs/mascot   another artist's SVG artwork, scraped and recoloured. Source material
#                 for the pixel data in MascotFrames, and not ours to redistribute.
#   docs/media    the phone photo the demo video is composited into, and the geometry
#                 notes measured against it. Instructions nobody else could follow, for
#                 rebuilding assets from one particular device.
#   tools         the scripts that drive that device: the keychain export helper (a
#                 working recipe for lifting a live credential off a machine), the
#                 recorder, the stills renderer.
#
# What the README displays lives in assets/ and is committed.
docs/
tools/

# ide
.idea/
*.hprof

# macos
.DS_Store

# generated media working files, and the local README render
.rear-demo/
.readme-preview.html

# Signing material. NEVER commit these — the release key is the one secret in this
# project that cannot be rotated: losing control of it means anyone can forge an update,
# and losing the file itself means nobody who installed the app can ever be updated.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
release.jks
